{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":105112,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,15]],"date-time":"2026-09-15T22:50:06Z","timestamp":1789512606837,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":50,"publisher":"AIP Publishing","issue":"20","funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/100011662","name":"Princeton Plasma Physics Laboratory","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["DE-AC02-09CH11466"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["DE-AC02-09CH11466"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100011662","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/100000001","name":"National Science Foundation","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["OIA-2217786"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["OIA-2217786"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100000001","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["pubs.aip.org"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,11,11]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>In the hexagonal, corundum-like structure, \u03b1-Ga2O3 has a bandgap of \u223c\u20095.1\u2009eV, which, combined with its relatively small electron effective mass, high Baliga's figure of merit, and high breakdown field, makes it a promising candidate for power electronics. Ga2O3 is easy to dope n-type, but impossible to dope p-type, impeding the realization of some electronic device designs. Developing a lattice-matched p-type material that forms a high-quality heterojunction with n-type Ga2O3 would open new opportunities in electronics and perhaps optoelectronic devices. In this work, we studied Ir2O3 as a candidate for that purpose. Using hybrid density functional theory calculations we predict the electronic band structure of \u03b1-Ir2O3 and compare that to \u03b1-Ga2O3, and study the stability and electronic properties of \u03b1-(IrxGa1\u2212x)2O3 alloys. We discuss the band offset between the two materials and compare it with recently available experimental data. We find that the Ir d bands that compose the top of the valence band in \u03b1-Ir2O3 are much higher in energy than O p bands in \u03b1-Ga2O3, possibly enabling effective p-type doping. Our results provide an insight into using the Ir2O3 or Ir2O3-Ga2O3 alloys as p-type material lattice-matched to \u03b1-Ga2O3 for the realization of p\u2013n heterojunctions.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1063\/5.0232445","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,11,11]],"date-time":"2024-11-11T11:12:32Z","timestamp":1731323552000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1063\/aip-crossmark-policy-page","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":9,"title":["Electronic properties of corundum-like Ir2O3 and Ir2O3-Ga2O3 alloys"],"prefix":"10.1063","volume":"125","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-3806-3827","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Shoaib","family":"Khalid","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Princeton Plasma Physics Laboratory 1 , P.O. Box 451, Princeton, New Jersey 08543,","place":["USA"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0358-2101","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Anderson","family":"Janotti","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Materials Science and Engineering, University of Delaware 2 , Newark, Delaware 19716,","place":["USA"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"317","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,11,11]]},"reference":[{"key":"2024111111122986800_c1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"719","DOI":"10.1021\/ja01123a039","volume":"74","year":"1952","journal-title":"J. Am. Chem. Soc."},{"key":"2024111111122986800_c2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"A316","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRev.140.A316","volume":"140","year":"1965","journal-title":"Phys. Rev."},{"key":"2024111111122986800_c3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"013504","DOI":"10.1063\/1.3674287","volume":"100","year":"2012","journal-title":"Appl. Phys. Lett."},{"key":"20